# synth/synth.ys -- generic (technology-independent) synthesis of the Phase 1
# tile, to confirm it's synthesizable and get real gate/cell-count numbers.
#
# Deliberately generic (Yosys's internal $_AND_/$_XOR_/etc. cell library, no
# `abc -liberty`): real physical area (um^2) and timing (delay/Fmax) require
# mapping onto an actual standard-cell library, which is Phase 3 (OpenLane +
# sky130) scope -- see the "Timing closure pass" Task Board card. This pass
# answers a narrower, still-real question: does the design elaborate and
# synthesize cleanly, and how many gates does it cost.
#
# Run: yosys -s synth/synth.ys   (from the repo root)

read_verilog -sv rtl/pe.v rtl/systolic_array.v
hierarchy -check -top systolic_array
proc; opt
synth -top systolic_array
tee -o synth/reports/systolic_array_synth.log stat
